2. Hardware — firmware/hardware/smart_energy_monitor/



config.h

All pins and ratings. Change relay polarity with RELAY_ACTIVE_LOW.

samplePower()





Battery voltage from a 10 kΩ / 3.3 kΩ divider on GPIO 35.



Current from ACS712-30A on GPIO 34 through a 1:1 divider.



P = V × I. If the divider is unplugged (V < 8), assume 12.8 V for USB tests.



decideLoads()

Same LDR / gas / SOC cutoff as Wokwi, but GPIO drives a 5 V relay (usually active LOW).

integrateSoc()

Blends measured watts with known lamp/purifier ratings. If battery > 13.2 V, treat the pack as charging and split generation 67% solar / 33% wind (highway pole: solar dominates). For a lab report, say this is an estimator until you add a second current sensor on PV.





3. Python logger — software/dashboard/energy_logger.py

Joins the same JSON /data and writes data/energy_log.csv. No pip packages required (stdlib only).





